  "rationale": "Lee Morgan's debut as a leader at age 18, already fully formed — a hard-bop landmark on Blue Note. AllMusic 3★ (a conservative rating for its importance). Quintet with Clarence Sharpe, Horace Silver, Wilbur Ware, and Philly Joe Jones — an A-list rhythm section that defines the Blue Note sound of the 1950s. Morgan is already in the canon with The Sidewinder, Cornbread, The Gigolo, and Search for the New Land; Indeed! captures his raw, brilliant arrival and completes the arc of his Blue Note leadership.",
